```console
$ scherzo-cloud project create --help
Create a project

Usage: scherzo-cloud project create [OPTIONS] --name <NAME> --installation-id <INSTALLATION> --repository-id <REPOSITORY> <ORGANIZATION>

Arguments:
  <ORGANIZATION>  Organization ID or exact slug

Options:
      --name <NAME>                     Set the canonical project name
      --installation-id <INSTALLATION>  GitHub installation binding ID
      --repository-id <REPOSITORY>      Provider repository ID
      --default-branch <BRANCH>         Set the configured default branch (the provider default when omitted)
      --pool-id <POOL>                  Runner pool ID or exact name
      --json                            Print the project result as JSON
      --service-api-key-file <PATH|->   Authenticate with a service API key from a private file, or - for standard input
      --allow-insecure-http             Allow this command's Scherzo Cloud requests over insecure HTTP connections
  -h, --help                            Print help

```
